commit b6609a289ab6c8392131bb06be40338c5ce5c225
Author: Nick <nick.eventslight@gmail.com>
Date:   Fri Aug 14 13:52:50 2026 +0200

    docs+hw: backup (2nd) USB3300 ULPI pinout, PCB requirements, diag tooling
    
    Document the backup ULPI breakout fully so the marginal-crystal lesson
    isn't lost:
    
    - README: new "Backup (2nd) USB3300 ULPI" section — bank-34 pinout
      (CLK=V4 MRCC, D-bus Y9/V8/W9/V9/W6/V7/Y3/Y6), build env flags
      (USB_BACKUP / NXT_W4 / USB_SWAP_D67), the NXT<->RST clock-pair swap
      rationale, and a PCB/hardware requirements block. Root cause of the
      whole bring-up saga was a marginal reference crystal (touch-starts,
      reflow-sensitive) -> load caps + cold-boot USB-PLL retry FSM are
      mandatory for a production board. Adds the clock-presence pass test.
    - Fix "free pins" list: Y3/Y4/Y6/W4 (+V4/R4/T5 + D-bus) now used by backup.
    - platform: USB_BACKUP=1 repins ULPI to the backup breakout; NXT<->RST
      swap keeps switching signals off the clock's differential partner (W4);
      uart_tx Resource on R3 for headless diagnostics.
    - Diag tooling: ulpi_clocktest_top.py (decisive V4 clock-presence test),
      ulpi_led_diag_top.py, ulpi_regread_uart_top.py + build drivers.
    - Bitstreams: backup-CLKTEST-v4.bit (pass test), backup-usb_utmi_ph0_READY.bit.
    - gitignore the diag build-output dirs.
    
    Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>

